=== layout: two-panels

# Talking Points Guide

@left

[*Edit and update your slide*]{color=#00775f}

- [*Images are required.*]{color=#003366} Add several pictures and some text.
- [*No complete sentences on slides.*]{color=#003366} Use short phrases and keywords.
- Be a visual storyteller. _You do the talking, not your slide._

@right

[*Content preparation*]{color=#00775f}

- Define the talking point, connect it to biotechnology, or give a recent example from biotechnology news.
- Try to be unique. Use the internet for research and provide your own perspective.
- Minimize jargon. Define technical terms your classmates may not know.

=== layout: one-panel

# Talking Points Guide

@body

[*Presentation delivery*]{color=#00775f}

- You have [*60 seconds per talking point.*]{color=#003366} Choose the most interesting part.
- Show *ENTHUSIASM* when you talk and make it exciting!

[*Put it in your own words*]{color=#00775f}

- It is okay to read from notes you wrote yourself.
- [*No direct quotes*]{color=#003366} from an article, Wikipedia, or the textbook.

