# Business Plan Extra Time

@body

{table-style=working}
| Students | Completion | Extra days | Example deadline |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | 0% | 0.00 | Dec 17 at 11:59pm |
| 1 | 8% | 0.04 | Dec 18 at 12:50am |
| 6 | 50% | 1.25 | Dec 19 at 5:59am |
| 8 | 67% | 2.22 | Dec 20 at 5:19am |
| 10 | 83% | 3.47 | Dec 21 at 11:19am |
| 11 | 92% | 4.20 | Dec 22 at 4:49am |
| *12 of 12* | *100%* | *5.00* | *Dec 22 at 11:59pm* |

@citation

Final grades are due from instructors at noon Thu, Dec 24, 2026.

@speaker-notes

The table shows the fewest students needed to reach each date, plus the result at full participation.
These examples assume a Dec 17 baseline at 11:59pm. The Fall 2025 workbook calculates extension days as
ROUND(5 * (students completed / class size)^2, 3) before adding them to the baseline.
Calculate extra days from the exact completion fraction. Round the displayed percentages to whole numbers
and the displayed extra days to two decimals. Announce the official deadline separately.

